{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541660-how-does-your-kindred-view-the-other-clans","id":1541660,"title":"How does your Kindred view the other clans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-06T13:03:39-07:00","id":1541660,"title":"How does your Kindred view the other clans?","content":"Just a fan experiment and I did a short version of it on another topic.<br /> <br /> I play mostly a 11th generation Malkavian networker who is from the Victorian Era and of course has dealt with nearly all the others at some point and came up with his notion. So here goes.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim. My Malkavian views them with wary interest and knows that they are more then warriors and have blood mages and vizers that could give the Tremere, Toreador and Ventrue some trouble down the road.<br /> <br /> The Brujah. Mostly disdain is what my guy feels as he trying to see where the Learned Clan part comes in and views them as bright stars that burn out quickly.<br /> <br /> The Caitiff: Mostly wonderment as how this group will pop up from time to time and makes the Kindred nervous.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel: My Malkavian doesn't deal with them much and just knows as tough survivalists that handle themselves.<br /> <br /> The Hecate: As far as he knows is that the Giovanni and a number of necromantic bloodlines somehow banded together for survival<br /> <br /> The Lasombra: Scary people who can use primordial darkness and only respect power is how my Malkavian sees them and acts accordingly<br /> <br /> The Ministry/Followers of Set. Sees them as a very adaptable clan that is overlooked by the rest of the Kindred and overlook how diverse there network of contacts are and they don't discriminate of whom they have in their pocket.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu: They may look horrible, but they are strong survivors with sharp ears and know things that can make all the difference and are willing to share for a price.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos: Not many of them around are they? <br /> <br /> The Salburi. My Malkavian has heard of them, but never dealt with them as far he knows.<br /> <br /> The Thin-Bloods: A group that even the Caitiff can feel superior to and should be watched carefully.<br /> <br /> The Toreador: Sees them as a waste of undead flesh that only like to think that they are the best of the best and that a bored Toreador is a very dangerous one.<br /> <br /> The Tremere: My Malkavian is glad is that they are mistrusted so much as they can see nearly as well my kindred's clan.<br /> <br /> The Tzismce: He isn't sure what to make of them as needlessly cruel fiends that revel in being inhuman monsters, which my Malkavian can respect<br /> <br /> The Ventrue: Kindred that see themselves as the rulers of undead society and have the power to back up the claim and try not to get them to angry in there domains.<br /> <br /> So that is how my character sees the other clans and I'm curious of how your player character sees it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T17:58:53-07:00","id":1541667,"title":"","content":"This is what my Nosferatu thought about then, I am taking be memory.<br /> <br /> Brujah: Dangerous, short-tempered and with varying levels of intelligence, but most do not have two functioning neurons. In some cases, likable. (Not the idealistic type)<br /> <br /> Ventrue: He is envious of them, of their status, of their money, although he wouldn't admit it, he want be one of then.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Depending on the night he hates them, feels sorry for them or would even accept traveling with a group of them.<br /> <br /> Toreador: Manipulators operating everywhere, with strange interests in humans, are by no means trustworthy. Really hate the clan.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: They are essentially poor souls who became informants out of necessity, some try to hide behind a facade, saying that this makes them strong and that anyone who underestimates them for being rabble will learn a bitter lesson. The truth is, that they are no more dangerous than other clans, they aren't as strong as the Brujah, they aren't as resilient as the Gangrel, they are not as resourceful as the Ventrue and Toreador, or even have anything unique like the Tremere, the best they know how to do is hide and any Malkavian functional enough would do the same. At the end of the day they are nothing more than the sewer rat clan. (He really didn't like be a Nosferatu).<br /> <br /> Tremere: He has some interest in Tremere sorcery, but more than that he is too pragmatic to learn anything from them and too fearful to try anything, so he keeps his distance from the clan.<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim: He sees them as professional killers, he heard some rumors about the clan, but he never felt like talking to any of them about what was true or not. Basically he fears then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T18:32:21-07:00","id":1541671,"title":"","content":"Sounds like my Malkavian would probably would have a good working relationship with your Nosferatu. I didn't add on how he views his own clan.<br /> <br /> My Malkavian comes across very &quot;sane&quot; but can display signs of obsessive behavior and tries to be mindful of of this issue as it could lead him into trouble that he can't get out of. In general he treats most if his clan with wary respect as they can see things that he might overlook.<br /> <br /> At times he does wish he was a member of The Ministry/Followers of Set clan and many Kindred in the world think he is a member of the Serpent clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-06-2024, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T15:27:34-07:00","id":1541706,"title":"","content":"Well, to my TC Tremere...<br /> <br /> Assamite: Religious idiots.<br /> <br /> Brujah: Angry idiots.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Feral idiots.<br /> <br /> Cappadocian/Giovanni: The idiots who taught me Necromancy. Gino and Lazarus are cool, though. Sucks Augustus flees the continent when he catches wind I'm around, the last time I was in the same room as him I got <i>this fucking close</i> to eating him and there wasn't a goddamned thing his entire clan and army of spectres could do about it. Just you wait until I get my hands on the Sargon fragment and manage to adapt the Spell of Life using the True Vessel as focus/sacrifice to resurrect my Daemon. I'm coming for your fat, incestuous ass, you disgusting fuck.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Eurotrash goth idiots.<br /> <br /> Malkavian: Crazy idiots.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: Ugly idiots.<br /> <br /> Ravnos: The really dumb idiots.<br /> <br /> Setites: lol<br /> <br /> Toreador: Pretentious idiots.<br /> <br /> Tremere: Yummy idiots. Fuck 'em all for falling for Saulot's bullshit. Becoming a true lich is just step one to usurping the clan and remaking it in my own...I mean, aiding my one and true clan founder in destroying Saulot once and for all, and bringing justice to the House's true betrayers. <i>Ahem.</i><br /> <br /> Tzimisce: The other yummy idiots (Vykos is cool though).<br /> <br /> Ventrue: Greedy idiots.<br /> <br /> <i>[Yes, I really did kick Augustus' ass once in that chronicle and he actually did run away any time my character was on the same continent. And I did have a plan to become a true lich...I just had to nail him down, eat him and drop to 3rd generation, learn Thaumaturgy and Necromancy 10, use the Sargon fragment to adapt the Spell of Life such that it could resurrect my character's Avatar, and then either eat or sacrifice the True Vessel as the primary ritual component.<br /> <br /> I explained every step to my ST in intricate detail, and even he had to concede my Tremere actually had a pretty good shot at pulling this off...the chief roadblock to my plan being Tremere himself, who wouldn't just allow one of his own subordinates to surpass him no matter how old or integral to the clan.]</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-07-2024, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T15:44:03-07:00","id":1541709,"title":"","content":"Sounds like your guy is typical Tremere.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T16:49:26-07:00","id":1541711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541660-how-does-your-kindred-view-the-other-clans?p=1541709#post1541709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like your guy is typical Tremere.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>...and my storyteller never let me forget it, believe me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T18:10:57-07:00","id":1541717,"title":"","content":"Here's another one, this time from a Gangrel, but he's not exactly sane.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: My clan, I'm grateful to my mistress for making me part of the &quot;family&quot; even if it wasn't planned. Before my embrace I would have thought that people like them were nothing more than stuck-up people who think they're the best, and some of them are, but over time I learned to survive, adapt, fight and also how important it is to have a pack, even if it's a headache sometimes and it was these guys who taught me that, sometimes I even forget that they could simply rip my head off.<br /> <br /> Brujah: A strong, united, brave group, in another life I might have been one of them, but they are foolish and quick to embrace lost causes, almost as much as they are to lose their patience. They are bearable most of the time, if you don't step on their toes, and despite everything they manage to make things work.<br /> <br /> Toreador (Females): They are the definition of the phrase: &quot;Roses have thorns&quot;. They are beautiful, smell good, well-groomed, talk well and are fun, they paint, dance, sing, I would easily fall in love with one of them and I would even like to, but despite everything, they lose interest in you easily. They are far from harmless, I have been shot too many times and cut too many times to believe that and even so it excites me instead of infuriating me.<br /> <br /> Toreador (Males): Idiots wanting attention.<br /> <br /> Tremere: I don't like them, they have their hierarchy, their rules and each one seems to respect it, even if reluctantly, which I don't understand, and on top of that they are very unpredictable, more so than the Malkavians, their magic doesn't seem to follow a pattern like the disciplines do and strangely they seem to like to annoy me with their secret schemes that lead nowhere.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu (Majority): I used to feel sorry for them, but not anymore, despite their appearance they are fighters, survivors and are far from weak. Rats are smart and can throw a punch when they need to, and I would even like them if I didn't have to go down to a stinking sewer to talk with one, and they can be jerks sometimes, I guess that's just part of who they are. Strangely enough, my mistress has mixed feelings about them, I wonder why.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu (Cleopatra): Crybaby.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: They call it the king's clan and they definitely act like it and they can certainly afford that arrogance. Apparently they have their own agendas and plans that I have no idea what they are, my mistress hates them, but I don't dislike all of them myself, rich friends are useful and they're not total jerks.<br /> <br /> Malkavian: My mistress mentioned that she once traveled with a bunch of them and that they were actually good company, until they had to kill them. I think there's something very wrong with that clan, I can't explain it, but they make my blood run cold, which shouldn't be possible.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: I haven't met many of them, but if you compare the impulsiveness of a Brujah and the arrogance of a Ventrue, you've got a Lasombra. I've never had a conversation with one, at least I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim: I haven't met many of them, and all the ones I've met have been at a safe distance. They seem quite sociable, even too much so for a kindred.<br /> <br /> Ravnos: They remind me a bit of my clan, especially when you consider that we share two disciplines in common. I've crossed paths with a few of them, they seem to be a very diverse group, but they all share a lack of attachment to rules, even those that are just common sense, which makes them a source of trouble, but I don't dislike them, I strangely feel a fascination for them. They seem to always be alone or in small groups, no more than three, I don't like to always be accompanied, but if I stayed alone for so long, I would feel suffocated, my lady says that this is the fate of all kindred eventually, it will be mine one day if I am not destroyed first. My second favorite I guess.<br /> <br /> It's the last time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T17:12:41-07:00","id":1541940,"title":"","content":"This is how my Brujah viewed the other clans.<br /> <br /> Brujah: This clan I was embraced into against my will as I drew the attention of a lovestruck neonate, We are called the Learned Clan and maybe in the past it was true but I see little of that now and when I try to aspire to such an ideal it feels like one step forward and three steps back.<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim: If they are in town, then you know that something serious is going to happen and some of us maybe become ash.<br /> <br /> Caitiff: Don't care for them and need to be kept in there place.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: You think your dangerous, I'll start to believe that if you can walk away from an encounter from this clan. I might be able to hit hard and fast and that means little to someone who can take incredible punishment and rend me into bloody strips.<br /> <br /> The Hecate: Being a Kindred is bad enough and these people make it worse by playing with ghosts and what else.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Anybody that can tear you apart from the shadows or rip your mind apart or match you in physical strength is someone to be respect.<br /> <br /> Malkavians: To unpredictable to work with on a regular basis and they seem to see things that are better left alone.<br /> <br /> The Ministry: Promptly pay back any favors and keep them at a arms length as they are always up to no good.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: I only get bothered by them when I don't see them in there usual haunts. If you don't see them at all then that means bad stuff is going to happen and you better hide yourself.<br /> <br /> Ravnos: Remember what I said about the Malkavians? These people are nearly as bad with the ability create illusions and they like to poke the bear way to much for my tastes.<br /> <br /> Salburi: Who?<br /> <br /> The Thin-Blood: To weak one on one to be a true threat, but when they pool there resources then watch out and there powers are surprising.<br /> <br /> The Toreador: What a waste of a clan that seems to be in love with there own reflections.<br /> <br /> The Tzmisce: Take the worst traits of despots and augment them and you get this clan of monsters who all seem to be sadistic and greedy to some extent.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue: The kings and queens of the night who try to rule our society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T05:33:54-08:00","id":1557414,"title":"","content":"My self insert Nosferatu would probably have the following opinions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos:</b> <i>&quot;Yes, I know you can't sleep within a mile of the same location more than once a week, I'm still not letting you inside to steal my shit!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Brujah:</b> <i>&quot;Your clan bane causes you to rebel just for the sake of rebelling. Which means all the trash talk clan Ventrue says about you is true.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra:</b> <i>&quot;Traitors! Cowards! Hypocrites! Get the fuck out of my domain, before I throw you out of it!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Banu Haqim:</b> &quot;The sheer gall of calling yourself Haqim's children, when you openly rejected him for the Camarilla.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tremere:</b> <i>&quot;Without the Pyramid monitoring your every thought, I'm willing to give you a chance... but know that I still don't fully trust you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hecata:</b> <i>&quot;You know the Giovanni didn't start as the dominant branch of your clan, right? But hey, if you fail to learn from history, that's your business.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Ministry:</b> <i>&quot;The fact that you are well known for distributing C.P makes the Anarch's willingness to accept you very alarming!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Toreador:</b> <i>&quot;I don't need beauty or good fashion sense to get laid. Blood bonds don't care how hideous you are.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T13:46:02-08:00","id":1557429,"title":"","content":"Play 2e but my current modern era Catiff/Bloodline Founder, she is in a version of the Chicago Chronicles and hasn't gone beyond the environs of Chicago and Garry since her Embrace<br /> <br /> Brujah: a mixed bag of Anarchists, Rebels without a Clue, Cult Leaders and out of touch Political Theorists, not counting the poor shmucks embraced on a whim of to fill some personal obsession, be careful many can slip in to the default personalty of Asshole, some choose it, others don't notice it still more fight it because it's not who they want to be, but it is a piece of them<br /> <br /> Gangrel: a collection of individuals, many are hippies and fringe dwellers, Respect them and leave them be, if you get to be palls it's on their terms.<br /> <br /> Malkavians: Leave Crazy alone, keep to at-least Minimum Safe Distance, some if not many are nice folks that don't mean no harm but there is something in their blood best left alone! but whatever the Blood has done to them can't be helped even if they mean nothing by it or are actively fighting it.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: Don't judge a book by it's cover, some are as twisted on the inside as they are on the out, others are some of the best of us, the rest are just Folk, that have bean dealt a poor hand.<br /> <br /> Toreador: <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Andr\u00e9</span> was one of them though he could at times be self absorbed, manipulative and pretentious he at least tried to be a good person. the same can be said for most of the Toreador they by and large are the most Human of the kindred for all our virtues and failings.<br /> <br /> Tremere: Plotting, Scheming, Deceitful, Manipulative, Power Hungry, Traitorous, UN-trustworthy C......'s, a few of their outsiders and fringe members are ok people but be careful the clan Elders have their hooks in to them and they can be made to turn on you at any time.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: collect all the Mobsters, Finance Bro's, Petty Autocrats, Egotists and sprinkle in a couple of Poli-Sic and Civil Admin Majors and you have Clan Ventrue. do your best to keep out of their way and avoid their infighting at all costs if you value your unlife. most seats of power have a Ventrue Ass firmly planted on them, when you must deal with them do it as quickly and without as much fanfare as possible, its best to let them take the credit most of the time and make sure they always get the blame unless it's a Tremere's fault<br /> <br /> <br /> Losumbra: the &quot;Antitrubune&quot; are up to something in their shadows, the Sabbat, for egalitarian revolutionaries they sure like to hold Court like some old world Aristocrat.<br /> <br /> Tzmisce: they are beyond Sick, something is deeply tainted about them, put their works out of their torments and burn any remnants of the Tzmisce themselves from their Flesh and Blood to the soil they need to rest in.<br /> <br /> Settites, Cultish Perverts, up to something, thankfully beyond in passing I've had nothing to do with them. <br /> <br /> Salburi: they feel like the Good Guys both the ones I've meet where real nice, help them when you can even if it's just to send a big F-U to the Tremere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28255-dropbear","name":"DropBear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T01:41:21-08:00","id":1557443,"title":"","content":"Sam loomis Sabbat Lasombra v20 with some 5th elements IC<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim/Assamites-the new name is pretentious and frankly, hardly cultivates trust but I digress, Excellent killers with all the personality of a brick.<br /> <br /> Brujah. They're at their most relevant when they're street muscle for us or the Tower, the Movement is a joke.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: excellent pack mates and born nomads<br /> <br /> Giovanni-never spoken with one.<br /> <br /> Lasombra- if we'd just stop getting in our own way we'd rule the world<br /> <br /> Serpents- competent mystics and vice peddlers. <br /> <br /> Nosferatu: They're not so bad, but it's really dumb how they bitch about how they look considering they're still vampires. It's like loosing a little finger for a billion dollars and getting hung up on the finger.<br /> <br /> Ravnos: incompetant mystics and vice peddlers.<br /> <br /> Salburi. Show respect.<br /> <br /> Thin-Bloods: I'm sorry but that's just a shitty version of a revenant. I'm not respecting you if you treat them like a peer.<br /> <br /> The Toreador: Oh it's the tzmisce but more creative and better in a fight, wonderful<br /> <br /> Tremere: The ones on the pyramid are formidably and respectable, the ones outside are a free generation buff.<br /> <br /> The Tzismce: Don't believe the ones who come across as normal, sooner of later that power gets them. Be polite and don't show fear.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue: Sabbat Ventrue are a more professional brujah/Salubri, encountering Tower Ventrue indicates you're winning the siege.<br /> <br /> Panders-I don't have any problem with the peasants as long as they don't get uppity. <br /> <br /> Blood brothers-Neat<br /> <br /> Harbinger of skulls-think tzmisce but with necromancy instead of torture","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T13:35:49-08:00","id":1557766,"title":"","content":"My revised Malkavian viewpoints on the other clans.<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim: They make the Ventrue, Toreador and Tremere nervous as they shown considerable skills in their chosen domains.<br /> <br /> Brujah: All sound and fury that means nothing and the few that are worthy of the title of the Learned Clan are to few to make a difference.<br /> <br /> Caitiff: I don't ignore these kindred as some of them have useful knowledge and skills that I can learn.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: I like this clan as they can get into places and travel more easily then I can and are deeper then most kindred realize.<br /> <br /> Hecata: The last couple of decades have been hard on the Giovanni and the other necromantic lineages as the SI and various agencies have hurt them and they had to put aside their differences to survive and one of them mentioned that they did a esotoric ritual to consummate the union. I still find them way to creepy for my tastes.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Remember what I said about the Hecata being creepy, this clan is more so because of there command over darkness and how ruthless they are.<br /> <br /> The Ministry: The so called High Clans love to overlook this clan as group of pagans, but don't understand how quickly they adapt and how diverse their group of contacts and how many of us owe them favours. I always did feel a kinship with this clan as it's said that our mutual antidulivans were close friends back in the ancient nights.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu: I find these folks have the best intelligence gathering network of all us and don't let the appearance disgust you as I find them more tolerable then most.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos: I'm so glad that this clan is almost gone as they did nothing but steal.<br /> <br /> The Salburi: I haven't to my knowledge ever encounter this clan and I have a hard time believing that they are still around.<br /> <br /> The Thin Bloods: At least the Caitiffs have someone to feel superior to, which isn't saying much.<br /> <br /> The Toreador: What a waste of vitae.<br /> <br /> The Tremere: How did putting clan before everything else work out for you?<br /> <br /> The Tzismce: They know much and honest about what they are, but I just wish that they didn't view me and others as possessions and not intelligent beings.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue: The lords and ladies of the night who can back up there claims of domain and remember to tread softly as you don't want a blood hunt called on you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-02-2026, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T03:32:06-08:00","id":1557775,"title":"","content":"<b>Here's the rest, from my self insert Nosferatu</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue</b> - <i>&quot;No, I don't have an army of soldiers ready to die in my service. But what I do have, is the names and addresses of all your preferred feeding vessels within the surrounding domain!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel</b> - <i>&quot;Yes, I know Protean can't make me prettier, that's not what I want it for. You see, I'm a fan of the classics, and I want the ability to turn into beasts and mist! Now, let's talk about making a trade!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce</b> - <i>&quot;Oh, how I envy your mastery over flesh. Alas, I lack the artistic skills and medical knowledge to wield such power myself.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Malkavian</b> - <i>&quot;The Camarilla calls us a 'death cult' when they let their lunatics wander around freely. At least we have the good sense to lock them in the dungeon when they're not actively deployed.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Caitiff</b> - <i>&quot;Personally, I think they're rather fascinating. But I'm still not recognizing them as a proper clan, no matter what that fucking Pander has to say about it.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Thinblood</b> - <i>&quot;Grab yer gun and hop in the truck, boys, we're goin hunt'n!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Camarilla:</b> <i>&quot;I've always wondered if vampire capabilities weaken from neglect, like mortals do. How long has it been since anyone on the Primogen has gotten off the couch to do some heavy lifting?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Anarchs</b>: <i>&quot;All you did was change the Camarilla's terminology, and hope we were too stupid to notice!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat</b> - <i>&quot;Path of Humanity not going as smoothly as you hoped? Maybe that's because you're not fucking human anymore, idiot. Come join our pack, we'll show you how to live as a vampire!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inconnu</b> - <i>&quot;What exactly is your deal again? One source tells me you want to seek Golconda, but another says you're a bunch of war mongers pitting the sects against each other.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Autarkis</b> - <i>&quot;If you have a shred of self preservation instincts, you will respect their elders. The rest are easy targets for diablerie.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T21:58:28-08:00","id":1557822,"title":"","content":"Other views from my Malikavian ancillea.<br /> <br /> Lupines: I rather greet a rising sun then fight one of these monsters.<br /> <br /> Mages: They might be mortal, but they have strange abilities to harm us and can move about in the daylight.<br /> <br /> The Fae: I don't know to much about them and I wonder if this is a case of maybe the dangers outweigh the benefits for me.<br /> <br /> Ghosts: They hate us for good reason and some of them can be quite dangerous.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs: Clueless youths who will become mommy and daddy sire in a few decades as they amass more power and don't want to share.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla: I know it's ruled by corrupt monsters, but this sect has been able to keep us safe from widespread exposure from the kine.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat: You stink of fear and envy of mortals and wage wars on beings who long since have forgotten about you.<br /> <br /> The Inconnu: I believe that this sect of potent Methuselah's and Elders do exist, but are used as a convenience when a kindred plot doesn't go the way they hoped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  I hate autocorrect. 02-02-2026, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T21:43:33-08:00","id":1558011,"title":"","content":"Yet more Nosferatu thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>Mages:</b> <i>&quot;How infuriating it must be for you. To possess the power of gods, yet are forced to kowtow to lesser beings.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves:</b> <i>&quot;What if I wear a paper bag over my head? No? Okay, fine, have fun pissing in the wind!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Fera:</b> <i>&quot;I know you probably hate me, but I still think you're cool!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Changeling:</b> <i>&quot;Stephanie Meyer called us fairies too, let me show you how I feel about that.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Demons:</b> <i>&quot;Why are you trying to convince me to sell you my soul, if I'm already inherently damned?&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-31T22:50:08-08:00","id":1558051,"title":"","content":"Low humanity Toreador: <br /> Brujah: Let your soul burn, firebrand.<br /> Gangrel: As the wind, or the storm.<br /> Malkavian: Dance with me.<br /> Nosferatu: I see you.<br /> Ventrue: Do not loose the things you have.<br /> Toreador: There's little left of me.<br /> Tremere: Is what you seek truly what you need?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-01T02:35:17-08:00","id":1558052,"title":"","content":"Italian Tzimisce Neonate, 1420, Road of Humanity, Doctor of Physik, Embraced in 1418 by a Tzimisce of the 7th Generation, Ghouled in 1415 by a Toreador of the 11th Generation. Moved cities at the direction of the Prince of Naples, to allow quarrels to resolve as swiftly as possible.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Brujah:</b></u> The Prince of Naples, Lo Stallone of Clan Brujah, in another life I would have been proud to be his Childe. He held in him everything the Clan should be; he was a philosopher, a king, a warrior, and on those rare occasions when it had merit, he was prepared to break beams and light fires for the sake of justice. He looked upon a walking crime, a stolen Ghoul embraced without permission, though with the complication of permission having been granted to a different sire, and he never showed me a moment's disrespect. If every Brujah were cut from that cloth, the world would be a better place.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cappadocians:</b></u> I know a Rabbi, elderly and decrepit prior to his embrace, and seemingly still infirm. He knows much, and shares a little. We will never agree on the nature of these 'wraiths' of his, but in him I see one face of a Clan of godly mystics, spending their nights tending to the dead. The Rabbi wanders the Jewish graveyard, and he remembers when the Jewish town was next door. He leaves the care of the living to others, something I'll never understand.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Malkavians:</b></u> Fools, high and low, blame madness on sin. God is not the cause, no, as with anything it is imbalance in the humours. The Malkavians understand this, and I have called on them to assist me in my work from time to time, patching injuries my hands cannot reach. Those which are sensible, worth talking to, are anything but 'Low', and can teach us much of the minds of Kine.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Nosferatu:</b></u> God forgive me, but I do struggle to look upon them. No mortal affliction can turn my stomach, my work is pus and bile, but the affliction of the Nosferatu goes far beyond their flesh. I'm told that Vicissitude can grant them beauty, but the curse reasserts itself, drags their flesh back into horrid shape. I should gladly spend weeks studying this, as awful as it would be, to deduce what enemy lurks in their skin.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Salubri:</b></u> We cannot lose them. Are the Princes mad? Does all Europe forget its Oaths, its Boons, its obligations? Would you listen to the propaganda of usurping diablerists?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Setites:</b></u> Two I have met. An old woman gripped with peasant superstition, but far kinder than the stories would suggest. She serves a remarkable blood beer at Elysium, with the Keeper's permission. The other is a merchant prince, and an enemy to his Clan. He is richer than the Pope, and says that Egypt is a land of evil, one he shall never visit again. If it weren't for his harsh words, meeting the matron might have left me certain that the Clan are being maligned as foreign, rather than being truly evil.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Toreador:</b></u> I hate to speak ill of my Domitor, and his Clan, but I have found them... frivolous. I play at frivolity, I tell the world I am a cad and a ne'er-do-well, and I spend my nights patching the poor's wounds. With the Toreador, what you see is what you get. My Domitor chose me for my looks, and I fornicated with him and his Coterie. They would gossip and argue like fishwives, each of them a woman after a fashion, and I don't think my skills or intellect ever played into me being groomed for the Embrace. At times I feel as if my Sire's crime freed me from an eternity of empty boasts.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Tremere:</b></u> Grubby, nasty, venal individuals from a grubby, nasty, venal bloodline. Clan! Even when I was a Toreador Ghoul, even before I became a Tzimisce, I knew them for what they are. Usurpers, criminals, charlatans. The Salubri are a noble Clan in the truest sense, healers all, and I would never trade High for Low.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Tzimisce:</b></u> I should sooner be a Dragon than anything else. Yes, there are many in my Clan, some quite close to me in blood, who use their gifts to twisted and ungodly ends. But hospitality, noblesse oblige, responsibility? These I hold dear. I am a doctor. <i>When it's nobody's business it's my business. I make it all my own, the villages, the land, the people, young and old. I hear the secrets they can't tell anyone else, I pull them from their mothers as they are born, I hold their hands as they die. I'm there when Priests and hope abandon them. I do it because it is right, because it is decent, and above all because it is kind.</i> Those are the words that drove my Sire to steal me, to embrace me. I hope that says it all.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ventrue:</b></u> I have taken a descendent of Mithras as my bosom friend and lover. He is young and thick-blooded like myself, and a chivalrous knight. I feel a kinship with him, a shared sense of obligation to the Kine and to the Low Clans, a sense of dignity and responsibility. His Sire is a colder fellow, distant and composed, lacking the warmth of compassion. I understand that he rules well, and so with the Ventrue I have no quarrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-01T04:36:17-08:00","id":1558053,"title":"","content":"Here's some I came up with for a Salubri Anarch.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu</b> - <i>&quot;I'm sorry, but your affliction is terminal.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce</b> - <i>&quot;Initiating quarantine safety protocols!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Banu Haqim</b> - <i>&quot;You exterminated our clan, because we were suspected of mass diablerie, but then welcome these guys into your Ivory Tower?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b> - <i>&quot;Normally, I use my healing arts to end people's suffering. But for you? I plan to extend it!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b> - <i>&quot;Let's see if your inner darkness can overpower my inner light.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ministry</b> - <i>&quot;They can give you what you want, but not what you need.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue</b> - <i>&quot;I don't know who's the bigger fools. You for allowing yourselves to be manipulated by the newly formed Tremere, or us for believing the Clan of Kings would be worthy allies?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Malkavian</b> - <i>&quot;Every time I try to rebuild your broken minds, there's always a critical piece missing from the puzzle.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Brujah</b> - <i>&quot;You come in here every month with a new petition against some perceived injustice. I'm not signing it this time!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Toreador</b> - <i>&quot;A willingness to treat people's suffering is not the same as being obligated to do so. Why don't we sit down and talk about the frequency of your visits?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel</b> - <i>&quot;Does acting like a wild beast alleviate the burden of consciousness?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Salubri</b> - <i>&quot;We can't afford to keep doing this Rule of Two nonsense, when our clan is on the brink of extinction. So get out there and start embracing!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Camarilla</b> - <i>&quot;Valeren is used to heal the body and soul. It won't do anything to repair your crumbling infrastructure.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Anarchs</b> - <i>&quot;I joined because they're less authoritarian than the Camarilla. Still think their methods could use some refinement, however.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat</b> - <i>&quot;Our Antitribu have every right to be pissed off, but that doesn't mean they should let their rage consume them.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T11:06:02-07:00","id":1562666,"title":"","content":"In the campaign i\u2019m part of, in Dark Ages, i\u2019m part of the Lost Tribe of the Banu Haqim.<br /> he pretty much admires all other kindred, unless they do something to him, or try to stop him.<br /> kinda works as i have a poor short-term memory, so don\u2019t always remember who has wronged him. <br /> if really bad i write it down\u2026 maybe i should create my own red list?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28559-malachy","name":"Malachy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28559_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}